%N A398101 Number of inequivalent n X n symmetric nonnegative integer matrices with each row sum nonzero and at most 2, up to simultaneous row and column permutations.
%H A398101 Andrew Howroyd, <a href="/A398101/b398101.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..1000</a>
%F A398101 G.f.: (1 - x)^2/(Product_{k>=1} (1 - x^k))^4.
%F A398101 a(n) ~ Pi^2 * exp(2*Pi*sqrt(2*n/3)) / (2^(3/4) * 3^(9/4) * n^(11/4)). - _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Aug 17 2026
%e A398101 The a(2) = 7 matrices are:
%e A398101   [1 0]  [1 0]  [2 0]  [0 1]  [1 1]  [0 1]  [0 2]
%e A398101   [0 1]  [0 2]  [0 2]  [1 1]  [1 1]  [1 0]  [2 0]
%t A398101 nmax = 50; CoefficientList[Series[(1-x)^2/Product[(1 - x^k)^4, {k, 1, nmax}], {x, 0, nmax}], x] (* _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Aug 17 2026 *)
